# Personal deployment checklist/notes — not project docs, never public.
# See SETUP-NOTES.md itself for what belongs here.
SETUP-NOTES.md

# backend/holdings.json is checked in on purpose — it's the worker's real
# input data (public, sourced figures about public people), and the
# automated workflow (.github/workflows/snapshot.yml) can't read it if it
# isn't in the repo. backend/state.json and backend/airports.csv are also
# checked in on purpose: the workflow commits them back to the repo itself
# after every run so state persists between runs — if they were gitignored,
# `git add` would refuse to stage them and the workflow's commit step would
# fail on every run.
#
# backend/snapshot.json really is a runtime artefact: it's copied to
# docs/snapshot.json (which IS committed and is what GitHub Pages serves)
# and the backend/ copy itself is never meant to be tracked.
backend/snapshot.json
backend/__pycache__/
